traint read is validated against the canonical bump before use (e.g. require!(stored == Pubkey::find_program_address(seeds, program_id).1))","the PDA (and its bump) is created in the same instruction using the canonical bump from find_program_address (NOT a caller-supplied bump passed to create_program_address, which accepts any valid off-curve bump and re-introduces the non-canonical-bump bug)"]},"severity":"WARNING","fingerprint":"requires login","lines":"requires login","validation_state":"NO_VALIDATOR","engine_kind":"OSS"}},{"check_id":"rules.solana-security-standard.sol-010-init-if-needed","path":"/src/src/lib.rs","start":{"line":284,"col":61,"offset":11919},"end":{"line":284,"col":80,"offset":11938},"extra":{"message":"Jelleo SOL-010: reinitialization / account takeover — matched on the PROPERTY, not one idiom. Fires on Anchor `init_if_needed` AND on a hand-rolled reinit: a raw account-header write via `.data.borrow_mut()` / `try_borrow_mut_data()`. If a permissionless handler (re)writes an account WITHOUT first proving it is FRESH (8-byte discriminator all-zero, `is_initialized == false`, or `#[account(zero)]`), a second call re-inits a LIVE account: the caller-chosen authority/owner overwrites the stored one, and a downstream `has_one = authority` instruction (withdraw/close) then trusts the attacker -> takeover -> drain. `owner == program_id` proves ownership, NOT freshness. SAFE form: read `data[0..8] != [0;8]` and reject an already-initialized account (Orca `initialize_dynamic_tick_array`), or plain `init` / `#[account(zero)]` + an existence guard checked before any payout. Real incident: Metaplex Candy Machine v1 config-drain. See: github.com/Copenhagen0x/solana-security-standard#sol-010.","metadata":{"sol-id":"SOL-010","category":"security","confidence":"LOW","technology":["solana","anchor"],"references":["https://github.com/Copenhagen0x/solana-security-standard#sol-010"],"license":"MIT","sss-tier":"high","sss-severity":"high","sss-exclusions":["the account holds no lamports, token balances, authority keys, OR access-gating state that a second initialization could reset — access-gating state includes (non-exhaustively) a timestamp / nonce / status used as a lock, AND any field that controls subsequent PDA derivation, account creation, or role assignment","an explicit already-initialized guard REJECTS a second initialization before any write — for a hand-rolled `.data.borrow_mut()`/`try_borrow_mut_data` write the 8-byte discriminator is asserted all-zero (`data[0..8] == [0;8]`) or an `is_initialized`/version flag asserted false and the handler returns Err when already set (Orca `initialize_dynamic_tick_array`), for Anchor it is plain `init` / `#[account(zero)]`; a bare `.data.borrow_mut()` that only writes a data region of an already-type-validated account (discriminator/authority untouched) also clears this","the value-moving path is gated by a nullifier/spent-marker created with plain `init` so a duplicate redemption ABORTS AT ACCOUNT CREATION before any payout - NOT a mutable boolean flag in an existing account (a flag a reset/reinit path can re-open does NOT clear this rule)"]},"severity":"WARNING","fingerprint":"requires login","lines":"requires login","validation_state":"NO_VALIDATOR","engine_kind":"OSS"}},{"check_id":"rules.solana-security-standard.sol-009-invoke-signed","path":"/src/src/lib.rs","start":{"line":327,"col":20,"offset":14040},"end":{"line":327,"col":34,"offset":14054},"extra":{"message":"Jelleo SOL-009: `invoke_signed` CPI. Verify the CALLER has authority for this operation BEFORE the CPI — `invoke_signed` just signs with a PDA, it doesn't validate upstream authority. See: github.com/Copenhagen0x/solana-security-standard#sol-009.","metadata":{"sol-id":"SOL-009","category":"security","confidence":"LOW","technology":["solana","anchor"],"references":["https://github.com/Copenhagen0x/solana-security-standard#sol-009"],"license":"MIT","sss-tier":"high","sss-severity":"high","sss-exclusions":["the caller's authority for THIS SPECIFIC privileged operation is verified (Signer + has_one/constraint binding the caller to the target resource) BEFORE the invoke_signed — a 'trusted target program' or any unrelated upstream Signer check is NOT sufficient"]},"severity":"WARNING","fingerprint":"requires login","lines":"requires login","validation_state":"NO_VALIDATOR","engine_kind":"OSS"}},{"check_id":"rules.solana-security-standard.sol-009-invoke-signed","path":"/src/src/lib.rs","start":{"line":334,"col":20,"offset":14261},"end":{"line":334,"col":34,"offset":14275},"extra":{"message":"Jelleo SOL-009: `invoke_signed` CPI. Verify the CALLER has authority for this operation BEFORE the CPI — `invoke_signed` just signs with a PDA, it doesn't validate upstream authority. See: github.com/Copenhagen0x/solana-security-standard#sol-009.","metadata":{"sol-id":"SOL-009","category":"security","confidence":"LOW","technology":["solana","anchor"],"references":["https://github.com/Copenhagen0x/solana-security-standard#sol-009"],"license":"MIT","sss-tier":"high","sss-severity":"high","sss-exclusions":["the caller's authority for THIS SPECIFIC privileged operation is verified (Signer + has_one/constraint binding the caller to the target resource) BEFORE the invoke_signed — a 'trusted target program' or any unrelated upstream Signer check is NOT sufficient"]},"severity":"WARNING","fingerprint":"requires login","lines":"requires login","validation_state":"NO_VALIDATOR","engine_kind":"OSS"}},{"check_id":"rules.solana-security-standard.sol-016-bump-field-read","path":"/src/src/lib.rs","start":{"line":376,"col":24,"offset":15179},"end":{"line":376,"col":30,"offset":15185},"extra":{"message":"Jelleo SOL-016: a stored `.bump` is read. Risk: a non-canonical bump — reused via an Anchor `bump = <account>.bump` constraint, or read and fed to `create_program_address` (both accept non-canonical bumps → PDA substitution). SAFE only if the SAME account's bump was set at init via Anchor's bare `bump`/`ctx